# RTK (Rust Token Killer)

When running CLI commands that produce verbose output, prefix them with `rtk` for 60-90% token savings. The output is compressed but preserves all actionable information.

## Auto-prefix these commands with `rtk`

- `rtk git status`, `rtk git diff`, `rtk git log`
- `rtk ls .`, `rtk read <file>`
- `rtk test <test-command>` (e.g. `rtk test cargo test`, `rtk test go test ./...`)
- `rtk lint <lint-command>`
- `rtk gh pr view`, `rtk gh issue list`

## Meta commands (use directly)

- `rtk gain` – token savings analytics
- `rtk discover` – find missed compression opportunities
- `rtk proxy <cmd>` – run without filtering (debugging)

## Do NOT prefix with rtk

- Interactive commands (editors, REPLs)
- Commands where exact output format matters (JSON APIs, jq pipelines)
- `curl`, `wget`, network requests
